<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lao People's Revolutionary Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1955–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as LPRP, Lao People's Party</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lao People's Revolutionary Party is the communist party that has ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> as the only legal party since 1975. It was founded in 1955 as the Lao People's Party, with roots in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochinese-communist-party">Indochinese Communist Party</a>, and led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a> in the civil war, taking its present name in 1972. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaysone-phomvihane">Kaysone Phomvihane</a> it abolished the monarchy, and it remains closely tied to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-vietnam">Communist Party of Vietnam</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lao-peoples-revolutionary-party.jpg" alt="Lao People's Revolutionary Party" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sshu94 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LPRP_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
